Our contributions:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{A black-box controlled framework} for per-axis style bias detection via style-controlled rewriting and position-controlled pairwise comparison (\S\ref{sec:method}).
    \item \textbf{The Likert Blindspot:} Likert scoring systematically misses style biases that pairwise comparison detects---complete at moderate bias ($d \to 0$ at $n = 355$), ${>}60\%$ attenuation at stronger effects---across six judge$\times$axis configurations ($p < 0.001$ pairwise vs.\ $p > 0.17$ Likert), confirmed by seven statistical methods (Tables~\ref{tab:main_results}--\ref{tab:sensitivity}); Likert-based audits may systematically underestimate bias.
    \item \textbf{Per-axis confound structure:} GEE decomposition shows verbosity is style-dominated (Style OR $8$--$13$, Orig OR ${<}1$), formality conditional, register judge-dependent---determining which estimates require conditional analysis (Table~\ref{tab:gee}).
\end{itemize}

